-- title:
--   Selfmaps generated by resolvents, composition and convex mixing
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a proof that every reflexive real Banach space has the fixed point property for nonexpansive maps: every $F:C\to C$ with $\|Fa-Fb\|\le\|a-b\|$ on a nonempty closed bounded convex set $C$ has a fixed point. The proof assumes a fixed-point-free map, reduces to a minimal invariant set $K$ of diameter $1$, builds an adaptive weighted tree of nonexpansive maps generated by resolvents, and contradicts the minimality through detecting functionals. Let $K$ be closed and convex and $T$ nonexpansive on $K$.
--
--   1. **Convex mixes.** For selfmaps $f,g$ and $a,b\ge0$ with $a+b=1$, $x\mapsto af(x)+bg(x)$. More generally, finite pointwise convex combinations $\sum_iw_ig_i$.
--   2. **Generated maps.** The smallest family containing the identity and all resolvents $R_n$, closed under composition and binary convex mixes. All generated maps are nonexpansive, and each has a finite displacement constant.
--   3. **Ambient image.** The generated maps viewed as functions $K\to X$. This set is convex and closed under finite convex combinations.
